<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-control-theory">
<title>Control Theory</title>

<introduction>
<remark>
<title>Prerequisites</title>
<p>Linear algebra, differential equations, dynamical systems, Laplace
transforms, optimization, numerical methods, probability, mathematical
modeling, and mathematical physics.</p>
</remark>

<remark>
<title>Learning Objectives</title>
<p>By the end of this section, the reader should be able to:</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>explain the purpose of control theory;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>distinguish open-loop and closed-loop control;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>identify plant, controller, actuator, sensor, input, output,
          disturbance, and reference signals;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>formulate state-space models;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>distinguish state variables from outputs;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand linear time-invariant systems;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>solve linear state equations using matrix exponentials;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand equilibrium points;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>linearize nonlinear systems;</p>
